his conference, (iv) this protocol does not uphold the high standard and obligations of the Convention on Cluster Munitions (CCM), (v) the development of a weaker legal norm with this protocol sets a dangerous precedent for avoiding existing legal obligations, and (vi) support for this protocol could potentially breach the obligations of a state party to the CCM; and (b) calls on the Government to: (i) recognise that the CCM is the reference for the prohibition of such weapons, and (ii) undertake not to support this protocol or any other instrument that weakens the CCM. Question put. The Senate divided. [15:44] (The Deputy President—Senator Parry) Question negatived.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-2130","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2011-11-01/1"}
